          "name": "Build a reusable context lens",
          "description": "Turn deterministic context selection into a reusable typed processor with a small public configuration surface.\n\nLesson: Expose a Context interface and selected controls; distinguish instance overrides, internal edits and saving a reusable shelf entry.\n\nLimitations: The lens selects supplied evidence; it does not restore omitted facts or write memory. Pinned internal edits use Make editable copy.\n\nOpening installs an unassigned copy. Bind local model roles and provide the documented evidence before running.\n\nPre: at most 1 auxiliary calls. Preview before publishing or applying.\n\nTry changing:\nOverride targetTokens from 720 to 420 on one lens and compare retained evidence; inspect that the saved definition stays unchanged.\nMake editable copy, change keepRecent from 2 to 1 and the protected pins, then Add to Subgraphs and Save new subgraph. Insert both versions and compare retained evidence.\n\nDocumentation specimen (does not seed chat or actor memory):\n\nSituation: Mira waits at the ferry gate with a sealed letter during inspection.\n\nGuidance: Keep inspection, letter and the latest question; plan one NPC response without assigning the player’s choice.\n\nRoot: acquire → process → publish: source.out → lens.context; lens.selected-context → plan.in; plan.out → publish.in. Root owns evidence and publication.\n\nInside: typed, reusable selection: Context enters and Context leaves. Expose four selection controls. Create a subgraph from the processor, then name its boundaries in Details.\n\nInspection · root evidence (source)\nPurpose: Read present evidence outside the reusable definition.\nInspect: Inspect supplied messages and character evidence; the lens receives a Context artifact.\n\nFerry-gate context lens (lens)\nPurpose: Place the pinned processor with deliberate instance settings.\nInspect: Open the wrapper. Exposed values target focus controls; source and publication remain root.\n\nEvidence in (lens.input)\nPurpose: Expose the named typed interface without a root source or terminal.\nInspect: Inspect artifact type, required status and the matching parent pin. Data boundaries preserve native record validation.\n\nKeep inspection and open question (lens.focus)\nPurpose: Select supplied Context deterministically using the recent-message protection, literal pins and token target; remove oldest nonmandatory messages first.\nInspect: Compare retained evidence and omissions. Select makes zero calls; maxTokens is inactive until compression is enabled. Purpose is inactive during deterministic selection and only guides the compression prompt. Purpose and the completion cap do not affect Select. Retention follows keepRecent, literal pins and oldest-message removal; semantic relevance belongs in a model-backed step.\n\nSelected evidence out (lens.output)\nPurpose: Expose the named typed interface without a root source or terminal.\nInspect: Inspect artifact type, required status and the matching parent pin. Data boundaries preserve native record validation.\n\nRespond at the ferry gate (plan)\nPurpose: Interpret selected evidence after the lens.\nInspect: Inspect a short playable direction tied to retained evidence. This is the one Analysis call.\n\nOutput tokens includes visible text and any reasoning tokens counted by the provider. A truncated result is discarded; inspect the error, then manually raise the cap and rerun. No automatic retry occurs.\n\nOffer the lens-based direction (publish)\nPurpose: Keep publication in the parent.\nInspect: Check the brief does not declare suggested actions already happened.",
